      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mt3rkqhdie5rkogl",
          "message": {
            "text": "Permanent suppression now requires every global-time partition to be known and disjoint. A null sweep mirrors Chromium’s false return and emits neither displayNone nor a visibility window; known intersections are reduced only to their conservative hull. The bottom-up walk unions that hull with every descendant before attaching an ancestor class, so ancestor visibility cannot suppress broader overflow/nested child paint. Focused tests reproduce the function-first negative-scale entry, the 50.5% crossing missed by N=50, and nested cancellation visible at 700 ms.",
            "markdown": "Permanent suppression now requires every global-time partition to be known and disjoint. A null sweep mirrors Chromium’s false return and emits neither displayNone nor a visibility window; known intersections are reduced only to their conservative hull. The bottom-up walk unions that hull with every descendant before attaching an ancestor class, so ancestor visibility cannot suppress broader overflow/nested child paint. Focused tests reproduce the function-first negative-scale entry, the 50.5% crossing missed by N=50, and nested cancellation visible at 700 ms."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/tree-ops/viewbox-culling.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 59,
                  "endLine": 76,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  const contexts = Array.isArray(ctx) ? ctx : [ctx];\n  const swept = conservativeSweptBoxes(staticBbox, contexts);\n  if (swept == null) {\n    // Mirrors Chromium's false-return contract: uncertainty keeps paint.\n    return { alwaysHidden: false };\n  }\n  const possiblyVisible = swept.filter((interval) =>\n    bboxIntersectsViewport(interval.bounds, vw, vh));\n  if (possiblyVisible.length === 0) return { alwaysHidden: true };\n\n  // One visibility class can express only one interval. Use the hull of all\n  // possibly-visible partitions; gaps remain visible (safe over-retention).\n  const visStart = possiblyVisible[0].startPct;\n  const visEnd = possiblyVisible[possiblyVisible.length - 1].endPct;\n  if (visStart <= 0 && visEnd >= 100) {\n    return { alwaysHidden: false };\n  }\n  return { alwaysHidden: false, visStartPct: visStart, visEndPct: visEnd };"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
